{
  "name": "exp_b_fixed_perworker",
  "_doc": "Exp B (raw throughput) + scalability — AR vs PS on MNIST/nielsen with a FIXED PER-WORKER batch of 64. This measures samples/sec and scaling as nodes grow, but the effective global batch changes with the worker count, so it is NOT a fair convergence comparison (only throughput). 8-epoch budget, no eval (throughput only). AR 1w is the single-worker reference for speedup.",
